; THE CONDOR — the size ladder's middle rung (GAMEPLAY-DESIGN V10). 1.2 m, 32 kg,
; and the frame that exists to answer "where is the sweet spot between a 5-inch
; quad and a manned machine".
;
; `hull` 100 and `evasion_style` jink for the same reasons as the Roc: V.q4 is
; open, so size stays the only variable, and no reference pilot has flown this
; airframe so its evasion identity is a default rather than a measurement.
;
; component_armor rotor 0.012 — PROVISIONAL, LIGHT (Iteration 17 / E4.2, authored
; from role per E.q7). A quarter of a raider bolt: a bolt strips 0.048 of rotor
; capability at the shipped severity, and 0.012 turns away a quarter of it.
;
; From role, not from a ratio. At 32 kg this is the first frame on the ladder with
; a real payload budget, so plating over the motor nacelles is something it can
; actually carry — and at 1.2 m it collects 37% of the rounds fired at it against
; the Kestrel's 8.7%, so it has a reason to. It is LIGHT rather than medium
; because it is the cheap workhorse of the ladder: an engineer protects it, they
; do not armour it the way they would armour the machine that costs fifteen times
; as much.
;
; THIS DOES NOT REOPEN THE `hull` DECISION ABOVE. Holding hull at 100 keeps SIZE
; the only variable for the scale yard, which is a FLIGHT comparison — nothing
; shoots at anyone there. Component plating is a different axis and does not enter
; that map at all.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="FrameConfig" load_steps=3 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://resources/frame_config.gd" id="1_frame"]
[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://resources/default_flight_condor.tres" id="2_flight"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_frame")
frame_id = &"condor"
display_name = "Condor"
flight_config = ExtResource("2_flight")
hull = 100.0
component_armor = {
&"rotor": 0.012
}
evasion_style = &"jink"
